From f3a9620d4559764295b78768933b2791326973fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 19:20:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/36] Preserve undefined lane definitions in identity copies

Reuse the prepared 0028 extraction as a compiler prerequisite. The
far-word boundary workload reaches its existing identity-copy lane
contract in word_pressure. The missing-patch compiler and pre-rewriter
MIR are retained; this is reconciliation of an existing root repair.

Pristine destination still removes the allocated identity copy without
remembering its undef-lane definition. Preserve the current
readsUndefSubreg(MI, MO) interface and the prepared generic X86 regression.

Prior extraction: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.0 (codex-tui), model gpt-6-astra,
xhigh reasoning effort; session 01a0db16-f6a0-7e32-ada6-0c8098813933.
Prior independent review: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1, model gpt-6-astra,
xhigh reasoning effort; session 01a0db96-a6cd-7800-82a5-6b871eb7e177.
Reapplication and validation: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (session source
vscode), model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session
01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84. Earlier implementation credits
remain in the canonical mos-coalescing-rc-undef record.
